0..79 Comment "// The circuit `H T H` runs on `|0⟩` to its exact amplitudes. No amplitude is"
80..91 Comment "// rounded."
92..94 Comment "//"
95..175 Comment "// A Clifford+T circuit takes amplitudes in the ring `ℤ[1/√2, i]`. A program"
176..253 Comment "// that rounds an amplitude to a float loses the equality of two states. Here"
254..327 Comment "// two equal amplitudes have one form, so a test compares states exactly."
328..330 Comment "//"
331..422 Comment "// `H T H` takes `|0⟩` to `(1 + ω)/2 |0⟩ + (1 − ω)/2 |1⟩`, with `ω = e^{iπ/4}`."
423..507 Comment "// The amplitudes are `(2 + √2 + √2 i)/4` and `(2 − √2 − √2 i)/4`. Their"
508..587 Comment "// squared moduli are `(2 + √2)/4` and `(2 − √2)/4`, and they sum to one."
588..590 Comment "//"
591..641 Comment "// - see: `../../../library/std/src/quantum.gandr`"
643..694 Comment "// The exact amplitudes and the gates on one qubit."
